+
+## KAMUN shared login — 28 October 2026
+
+Approved workflow: one personal ECE-issued code in KAMUN identifies the delegate committee-country or the individual chair committee/role. A private HTTPS endpoint verifies that identity; a one-minute, single-use ticket opens ECE as the same person without entering the code again. The normal ECE HTTP-only cookie remembers access until its configured expiry. An existing different-account cookie must not take precedence over the handoff. KAMUN does not store the reusable code or ECE login pepper.
+
+This restores the integration reverted in a59a9af in a separate branch. Participant and staff endpoints use a separate KAMUN_INTEGRATION_KEY; the staff endpoint can notify KAMUN_REVOCATION_URL on credential changes. Secrets and environments must be paired explicitly. This branch is not a deployment.
+
+Linked tickets and sessions carry an opaque installation scope derived server-side by KAMUN from its Supabase project, conference and user ID. KAMUN logout invalidates its binding, then asks the private ECE endpoint to increment that scope's generation and remove its tickets and sessions. Ticket consumption checks the generation atomically when creating a session, preventing a concurrent exchange from surviving logout. Independent device sessions are unaffected. This does not revoke unrelated ECE sessions created by entering a code directly. ECE logout still affects its own cookie; it does not sign out KAMUN.
+
+Deploy additive migrations 0011 and 0012 and the new participant/staff code together with KAMUN's claim, refresh, handoff, logout and revocation functions. Rehearse on fake staging accounts. Never run provision:demo as part of deployment or import the existing real code roster into another database. The connected account in this session cannot deploy the friend's live domains.
+
+### Participant back navigation — 2026-11-04
+A 44px back-arrow button above the participant header returns through browser history without signing out. It is disabled when the tab has no previous history entry. When ECE is opened from Kamun in the same tab, it returns to Kamun; no destination URL or credentials are added to the link.
